        "id": "p18-q15-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Prove that $\\triangle ADE$ is similar to $\\triangle ACB$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\triangle ADE\\sim\\triangle ACB$ (AAA).",
          "worked": "Since DA and DB are opposite rays, $\\angle ADE+\\angle EDB=180°$. The given condition is $\\angle ACB+\\angle EDB=180°$, so $\\angle ADE=\\angle ACB$. Also $\\angle DAE=\\angle CAB$ is common. Therefore $\\triangle ADE\\sim\\triangle ACB$ by AAA, matching D with C and E with B.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 17
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q15-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Prove that $\\dfrac{AE}{AB}=\\dfrac{AD}{AC}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{AE}{AB}=\\dfrac{AD}{AC}$.",
          "worked": "In the similarity ADE~ACB, AE corresponds to AB and AD corresponds to AC. Corresponding side ratios therefore give $\\frac{AE}{AB}=\\frac{AD}{AC}$.",
